Description: Fix Linlon decoder lifecycle, EOS and capture buffer ownership
 Handle color-description and EOS notifications without treating valid events
 as failures. Validate VDEC lifecycle calls and fail cleanly on permission or
 module initialization errors. Latch output EOS at capture LAST, serialize
 request/return/flush ownership, and make stale post-flush returns idempotent.
 Every OK, NULL_DATA or ERROR_FRAME capture dequeue transfers ownership to the
 caller and requires a return; repeated zero-length initialization buffers
 must be requeued. Initialize capture ownership after codec and stream setup.
 Native H.264 multi-epoch plus VP8, VP9 and HEVC tests require this k3.8 state
 machine.
Author: Yeqin Su <hougelangley1987@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-19

